# swiftformat config for Put
--swiftversion 6.0
--indent 4
--maxwidth 120
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections before-first
--closingparen same-line
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--self remove
--semicolons never
--trailingclosures
--commas inline
--elseposition same-line
--operatorfunc spaced
--nospaceoperators ...,..<
--ranges no-space
--emptybraces no-space
--patternlet hoist
--redundanttype inferred
--shortoptionals always

# Both rules became defaults in SwiftFormat 0.62 and would rewrite every
# single-line `if x { return }` guard in the codebase onto three lines. That
# one-line form is the established style here, so the rules stay off - which
# also keeps lint deterministic across formatter upgrades instead of depending
# on whichever version the machine or CI runner happens to install.
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies
